WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:01.750
Saffron,

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:02.930
beluga caviar,

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:04.000
truffles,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.270
and Bonnotte potatoes

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.910
are just some of the world's
most expensive foods.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.530
Wait, potatoes?

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.660
Is that right?

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.880
Guys, it says here on
the script "potatoes."

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.250
A Potato?

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.173
Seriously?

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.040
Welcome to Noirmoutier.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.210
A tiny island off the
Atlantic coast of France.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.560
This is the only place you
can find the king of potatoes.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.260
His majesty, La Bonnotte.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.810
But if you want to eat them
fresh you've got to be quick

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.460
as they're only available
for 10 days a year.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.580
This is Rudy.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.380
He's a potato farmer.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.250
So what makes the island of Normoutier

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.323
so special for these spuds?

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.530
All the farmers on the island
are part of cooperative.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.620
They deal with treating,
cleaning, selling,

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.513
and sending all over Europe.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.110
Nicholas is the director.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.510
He makes sure everything runs smoothly.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.293
He really loves these potatoes.

00:01:20.444 --> 00:01:25.444
Sorry.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:41.130
Now, I hope you're sitting
down because in 1996

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:45.020
these pricey potatoes fetch
at auction an insane amount.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:45.853
Drumroll!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.380
Roughly $500 per pound.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.270
Luckily, for you and me,

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.310
nowadays, Bonnotte potatoes
aren't going to break the bank.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.230
Fetching more like 5 dollars per pound,

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:00.933
which is still a lot
for a bag of potatoes.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.850
Once the harvest is complete

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.920
an annual Bonnotte festival is held.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.330
Here, the golden potatoes
are traditionally served

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.870
with grilled sardines.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.603
So how do they taste?

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.530
So there we have it.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.270
The king of potatoes.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.970
Thank you, Your Majesty.

